# Development

Initialize the module with `go mod init {{project_slug}}`, or use the intended
remote module path and replace `{{project_slug}}/internal/` in the Go imports.
Resolve the dependencies before running the Makefile:

```sh
go get github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk github.com/stretchr/testify
go mod tidy
make install
```

Install golangci-lint using its official instructions and write its installed
version to `.golangci-lint-version`. Run `make help` for every target.

```sh
make fmt-check tidy-check vet lint build test test-integration smoke coverage
go test -race -run TestConvertUnitsToolErrors ./internal/server/
```

## Trying the server

The server speaks JSON-RPC on stdin and stdout, so run it through a client:

```sh
make call                                                     # list the tools
make call TOOL=convert_units ARGS='{"value": 5, "from": "km", "to": "mi"}'
```

`make call` builds the binary and runs `cmd/mcpcall`, which starts it the way
a host does. Piping hand-written JSON-RPC into the binary prints nothing: the
server stops when stdin closes, before it replies. The MCP Inspector's web UI
(`npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector ./bin/{{project_slug}}`) is for a person
at a browser; its `--cli` mode works from a script.

## Stdout

Stdout is the transport. golangci-lint's forbidigo rule fails on
`fmt.Print*`, `println`, `os.Stdout` and the standard `log` printers outside
`cmd/mcpcall`; the integration test fails if any stdout line isn't JSON-RPC.
Log through the `*slog.Logger` passed down from `internal/app`.

`make test`, `make test-integration` and `make coverage` use `-race`, which
needs cgo and a C compiler.
